# SLOW: loops over every previously placed queen on every safety check
def is_safe(row, col, placement):
    for r, c in enumerate(placement):
        if c == col or abs(r - row) == abs(c - col):
            return False
    return True
```

This version is correct, but every call costs O(row) instead of O(1), and it's called for every column tried at every row — so the constant-factor cost compounds across the whole search rather than being a one-time inefficiency. On small N the difference is invisible; past roughly N=10-12, the rescan version becomes noticeably slower than the set-based version doing the identical logical check, purely from the wasted repeated work.
